## Decision process

- Routine changes: one maintainer review + green CI to merge.
- **Releases require two maintainers to approve** (Q26). Until there are at least
  two maintainers, releases are cut by the project lead with a recorded rationale.
- Material changes to public contracts (IR, artifact schemas, journal format,
  public APIs, plugin manifests) follow the compatibility and deprecation policy
  in the PRD (§5.9, §16.6, Q29) and are called out in the CHANGELOG.

## Governance evolution (Q26)

At 1.0, or once there are five external maintainers, the project moves to a
steering group of at least three maintainers.

## Security & disclosure

A security team of at least two people handles reports via the private advisory
channel with 90-day coordinated disclosure (see [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md), Q26).

